  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">WFP integrated food security project in Uror, Nyirol, Duk and Bor counties.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This World Food Programme (WFP) project will assist 219,252 vulnerable women and girls, returnees and internally displaced persons affected by crises in Uror, Nyirol, Duk and Bor Counties of Jonglei State in South Sudan with General Food Distribution (GFD) and Blanket Supplementary Feeding (BSF) through provision of nutrition -sensitive food assistance (In -Kind).  Beneficiaries (20,358) will also be engaged in Asset Creation and Livelihoods (ACL) activities, and they will receive either cash or in -kind support.  The project also has a School Feeding (SF) component aimed at improving enrolment, attendance, and gender disparities of 6500 boys and girls in 9 targeted schools in Uror and Nyirol counties by December 2024 through provision of daily hot school meals. The project runs from 1 January 2024 to 31 March 2025.</narrative>
  </description>
